 '[{"text": "Yes, since AB + BC = AC (5 + 5 = 10)", "feedback": "Correct. AB = √(3²+4²) = 5, BC = √(3²+4²) = 5, and AC = √(6²+8²) = 10 — since AB + BC = AC, B lies exactly on segment AC, so all three points are collinear."}, {"text": "No, since AB ≠ BC ≠ AC", "feedback": "AB and BC actually come out equal here (both 5) — recompute both using the distance formula before comparing."}, {"text": "Yes, since AB = BC", "feedback": "AB and BC being equal only shows B is equally far from A and C — collinearity needs AB + BC to equal AC, which is a separate check."}, {"text": "No, not enough information to tell", "feedback": "The distance formula applied to all three pairs of points is exactly enough information to decide this."}]'::jsonb,
