 '[{"text": "k = 3 or k = 7", "feedback": "These reuse numbers already in the problem rather than solving √((5−k)² + 4²) = 5 for k."}, {"text": "k = 2 or k = 8", "feedback": "Correct. √((5−k)² + 4²) = 5 leads to (5−k)² = 9, so 5−k = ±3, giving k = 2 or k = 8."}, {"text": "k = 1 or k = 9", "feedback": "Close, but recheck (5−k)² = 5² − 4² = 9 — these values give a difference of 4 from 5, not 3."}, {"text": "k = 0 or k = 10", "feedback": "These give (5−k)² = 25, which is 5² itself — the 4² from the y-difference still needs to be subtracted first."}]'::jsonb,
